From: Project contributors <contributors@example.invalid>
Subject: meson: prefer the machine-file python

Mesa probes versioned interpreters (python3.16, python3.15, ...) before
"python". When the build host ships a newer interpreter than the one the
build system stages, meson picks the host one while PYTHONPATH still points
at the staged standard library, and the code generators fail inside
importlib. Look up "python" first so the [binaries] entry of the native or
cross file wins; the version and mako checks below still apply to it.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1090,7 +1090,7 @@ endif
 # - On Windows, a venv has no versioned aliased to 'python'.
 # - On RHEL 9, python3 is 3.9, so we must use python3.12.
 python_version_req = '>= 3.10'
-python_exec_list = ['python3.16', 'python3.15', 'python3.14', 'python3.13',
+python_exec_list = ['python', 'python3.16', 'python3.15', 'python3.14', 'python3.13',
                     'python3.12', 'python3.11', 'python3.10', 'python3', 'python']
 
 foreach p : python_exec_list
